 ],
 "notes": "Trust-policy checks read the role's planned assume_role_policy, the declared inline text, or an aws_iam_policy_document the role references; a trust policy held only in a local (DSV4F) is invisible and fails them. The OIDC provider's own client_id_list/url no longer count as trust-policy conditions. No candidate writes the issuer (:iss) condition the prompt asks for (cond_iss kept). no_managed_policies selects every role plus any attachment resource and requires that no attachment exists in the default plan and the role sets no managed_policy_arns. An explicit managed_policy_arns = [] (planned as an empty list) would fail no_managed_policies; unset or unknown passes."
}